<title>USA: Dunavant sees March cotton in 73-76 cent range.</title>
<headline>Dunavant sees March cotton in 73-76 cent range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Closely watched cotton merchant William B. Dunavant Jr said the March 1997 cotton futures contract on the New York Cotton Exchange is likely stay in a range between 73.00 and 76.00 cents a lb for the remainder of the crop year.</p>
<p>In a speech at the annual Beltwide Cotton Conferences, Dunavant said producer selling beginning at 76.00 cents could limit an upward move.</p>
</text>
